; A runtime-computed key query reaching GPU code — rejected. The general
; String gate catches it first (`CPUExclusiveTypeInGPUEntryPoint`: a
; non-literal key is a String-typed expression, and Strings are
; CPU-exclusive wholesale); `GpuKeyQueryRequiresLiteralString` remains
; as `validate_gpu_window_info`'s backstop behind it. GPU key queries
; compile into one implicit uniform binding per distinct compile-time
; key, so a dynamic key could never bind regardless. On the CPU the
; same expression is a legal live query (see the
; `dynamic_key_query_spoofed` buffer test).
@storage-write
(var out: [1: f32])

@compute
(defn probe []
  (= (out 0u)
     (if (key-down? (string 3u)) 1. 0.)))

@cpu
(defn main []
  (spawn-window (fn []
                    (dispatch-compute-shader probe (vec3u 1u))
                    (close-window))))
